 ## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
 
 - **No fuzzy content search or event deep links** — the content backend uses literal token/phrase matching, and selecting a result opens the Session rather than the matching event.
-- **No Session deletion or unarchive control** — sessions can be archived, but archived sessions have no viewing or unarchive surface, and Workspace registration deletion does not delete Sessions.
+- **No unarchive control or attachment garbage collection** — archived sessions have no viewing or unarchive surface; permanent Session deletion intentionally retains shared content-addressed attachment blobs until a reference-aware garbage collector exists.
